{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"censorious-stinky-tortoise","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/unit cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/_opcert_helpers.py:1-8, 30-36` — Preserve storage-anchor/ordered-chain fixture contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/conftest.py:1-9, 22-27, 29-38, 40-58, 81-84, 87-88, 102-121, 138-157, 184-210` — Preserve import-order invariants and hermetic session-log/MCP/AWS isolation. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/gold_set_completion.py:1-24` — Preserve the frozen labelled completion-floor corpus semantics. Consumer: calibration-script and test maintainers (the module data is imported, the prose is not).\n- `tests/unit/test_8d44_cache_attestation_freshness.py:1-16, 69-70, 82-85, 93-95` — Preserve cache/evidence consistency invariant and tampered-cache fixture shape. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_a8e5_absence_veto_edge.py:83-88` — Preserve false-vs-genuine absence contrast. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_ac_satisfiability_criterion.py:1-10, 30-37, 126-132` — Preserve criterion gap, routing tier, and end-to-end wiring. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_administrative_close_dispositions.py:1-20` — Preserve admitted classes, reason/link requirements, and signed-disposition behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_advanced_cli_parsers.py:1-13` — Preserve parser-factory and lazy-import contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_agent_call_memo_nudge.py:1-15, 378-382` — Preserve caching eligibility, error handling, guard ordering, and path-normalized reads. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_agent_call_runaway_guard_c827.py:1-10` — Preserve abort thresholds, typed failure, and healthy-control behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_agent_call_seam.py:1-13` — Preserve extracted seam contracts and leaf constraint. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_agent_skill_ticket_workflow_guidance.py:1-10` — Preserve which workflow behaviors the tests guard; delete ticket-by-ticket genealogy and `compress`. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_agentic_budget_and_truncation.py:1-15` — Preserve configured budget propagation and unretryable truncation behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_agentic_message_cache.py:1-33, 238-241, 259-261, 314-320, 397-401` — Preserve provider-specific cache-point contracts, frozen pre-fix control, and three-point limit. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_agents_claim_assignee_guidance.py:1-11` — Preserve omitted-vs-explicit assignee behavior and Jira identity constraint. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_agents_serena_untyped_receiver.py:1-13, 59-62` — Preserve `Any` receiver blind spot and real three-site census. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_alarm_actions_terraform.py:1-35, 49-53, 422-427, 478-481` — Preserve alert-action, missing-data, anti-vacuity, and AWS length constraints. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_amend_msg_change_id.py:1-21` — Preserve why a wrapper is required, Change-Id preservation, and negative control. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/_opcert_helpers.py tests/unit/conftest.py tests/unit/gold_set_completion.py tests/unit/test_8d44_cache_attestation_freshness.py tests/unit/test_a8e5_absence_veto_edge.py tests/unit/test_ac_satisfiability_criterion.py tests/unit/test_administrative_close_dispositions.py tests/unit/test_advanced_cli_parsers.py tests/unit/test_agent_call_memo_nudge.py tests/unit/test_agent_call_runaway_guard_c827.py tests/unit/test_agent_call_seam.py tests/unit/test_agent_skill_ticket_workflow_guidance.py tests/unit/test_agentic_budget_and_truncation.py tests/unit/test_agentic_message_cache.py tests/unit/test_agents_claim_assignee_guidance.py tests/unit/test_agents_serena_untyped_receiver.py tests/unit/test_alarm_actions_terraform.py tests/unit/test_amend_msg_change_id.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"0302-f5d0-aa57-4d5c","parent_id":"ae4d-df34-480d-4c88","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/unit — cohort 01: opcert_helpers–amend_msg_change_id"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788571243306670953,"uuid":"776cca62-578c-41ce-8c90-22c8adf182d2"}